From 45d0c0592eed96cb969b0c7b65f7dd42e3877ca2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: irregularthanis <343663069+irregularthanis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 08:05:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 197/205] Aurora: count Smooth Motion's overloads by cause and
 time the in-between replay

note_overload takes a typed cause and the wait that found it. stats() counts
each cause's overloads and waits, each presenting frame's verdict (delivered,
skipped, cut, rejected, idle or unstaged) and pacing's budget changes;
DOL_AURORA_FRAME_INTERP_STATS=1 logs them each second as [interp-stats].
The in-between replay gets a [gpu-prof] frame of its own with an
"In-between replay" zone. Pacing itself is unchanged.
